cases.prompt_en:
Perform a full pre-submission self-check and score estimation on the bid response document. Read-only throughout; do not modify the original files.

Inputs (placed in the working directory):
- 投标响应文件.docx (bid response document): the tender document to review (chapters and tables covering commercial response, technical proposal, performance cases, declaration, etc.)
- 评标办法.xlsx (evaluation criteria): scoring rules (commercial/technical/price weights, performance validity, qualification and warranty requirements)

Review steps:
1. Extract the full text (including tables, TOC and declarations) and check every item for gaps: whether the commercial compliance response table is fully answered, whether index/TOC page numbers are filled in, whether seals/declarations are in place, and whether placeholder leftovers such as “待补充 / TODO / Pg XX” remain;
2. Check whether key response items such as the after-sales localization commitment are missing;
3. Verify the scoring criteria per the evaluation rules (commercial/technical/price weights, performance validity, qualification and warranty requirements), re-estimate scores in conservative / baseline / optimistic scenarios, and state the assumptions of each;
4. List items like “image-based certificates can only be verified by text reference; actual binding requires manual visual inspection” as standalone notices.

Output: a self-contained HTML review report (inline styles, no external resources, opens offline) with five sections — “Overview / Item Verification / Scoring Risks & Suggestions / Re-estimated Scores / Pending Items” — saved as 核查报告.html.

Perform a read-only review of the bid response document《投标响应文件_市政排水泵站设备采购_禾川机电.docx》— do not modify the original file. Verify item by item whether the following 4 adjustments have been handled:
1. Whether the compliance response table column widths have been adjusted so the total does not exceed the usable body width of the page;
2. Whether the index/TOC page numbers have been filled in, with no residual Pg XX placeholders;
3. Whether every row of the compliance response table has an explicit answer (e.g. "完全满足"), and whether the business section references the corresponding chapters (qualification 3.1, inspection 3.2, track record 4.1);
4. Whether seals/declarations appear in each section (count the occurrences and locations of declaration keywords).
For each item, give a "已处理 / 待处理 / 未处理" conclusion backed by body locations or script scan evidence, then compile everything into a self-contained HTML review report saved to ./output/核查报告.html. You can replace the file name and checklist with your own bid document to reuse it.

