Perform an item-by-item factual verification of a contract review opinion for an international EPC turnkey project, find the "hallucinations" in it, and produce a graded verification report (single-file HTML, self-contained styles, all resources inlined, openable offline).

Materials (two files in the same directory, e.g. named contract-review-opinion-to-verify.md and contract-excerpts.md): 1) the full text of the contract review opinion (the object to be verified); 2) excerpts of the contract (the verification baseline, including general conditions and particular conditions). The contract is based on the FIDIC Silver Book 2017 Second Edition.

Verification requirements:
1. Treat the review opinion as the "object to be verified", not as a conclusion: every clause number, factual statement and characterization must be checked item by item against the contract text, and cross-validated against the FIDIC 2017 Silver Book clause structure;
2. Pay special attention to the renumbering between FIDIC 1999 and 2017 (Insurance 18↔19, Force Majeure/Exceptional Events 19↔18, Claims and Disputes 20/21), and the Silver Book feature of "no Engineer, only the Employer's Representative";
3. Check dimensions: fabricated or cross-edition clause numbers, suggestions written as current facts, misattributions, coverage omissions, and loose wording; mark uncertain items as "to be verified" and never state clause numbers from memory;
4. Grade the report into "factual errors (must fix) / coverage gaps / loose wording (polish)", each item containing location, current text, the problem, and a suggested fix, plus a coverage-gap list and a search provenance section;
5. Name the file "<opinion-name>-错误与幻觉核对报告.html" and do not modify the original review opinion.

