I'm 35, a senior backend engineer at a top tech company with a total annual package of about 800K RMB. I have a mortgage and a child, my family has another stable income, my available startup capital is about 1.2M RMB, and my risk tolerance is medium. I'm torn over whether to quit and go all-in on an AI application startup.

Please use your High-Dimensional nine-step decision method to produce a complete decision analysis:
1) First use Cangjie encoding to redefine my vague anxiety into the real problem to decide;
2) Use Yin-Yang dialectics to list both sides (pros/risks) and the key conditions for Yin-Yang transformation;
3) Use systems science to analyze the relationships and feedback loops among technical ability, product commercialization, cash flow, and mental energy, and point out the real bottleneck node;
4) Use the Kondratieff cycle to judge which phase the AI track is currently in, and give the matching cycle strategy;
5) Use a world model to give optimistic/base/pessimistic future scenarios with their probabilities;
6) Design at least 3 options (including all-in, moonlighting-first, and a curved entry), listing core idea, expected return, main risks, and suitable conditions;
7) Use the Nuwa paradigm to give a recommended option (with core reasoning, key success factors, and an emergency stop-loss plan);
8) Provide a three-phase action roadmap (0–30 days / 1–3 months / 3–12 months) and a feedback/retrospective mechanism;
9) Finally, do a cosmic-view value calibration reflection.

Please turn the result into a polished, readable single-file HTML decision report: light professional style, clear information hierarchy, with Yin-Yang comparison cards, a Kondratieff cycle timeline, scenario probability bars, an options comparison table, an action timeline and other visual elements; it must be a single file with all CSS/JS/image resources fully inlined, openable offline, and referencing no external links.

