cases.prompt_en:
ASCO 2025 just wrapped and the team came back with a pile of screenshots, but nobody can say which conclusions will actually change clinical decisions tomorrow. Build me a "topic radar" for lung cancer.

Here is what was publicly reported at the meeting, as a starting point:
Publicly reported highlights from the 2025 ASCO lung cancer sessions:
SACHI, led by Prof. Shun Lu (MET-amplified population; osimertinib plus savolitinib vs platinum-doublet chemotherapy; median PFS 8.2 vs 4.5 months in the ITT population, ORR 58%; median PFS 6.9 months in the third-generation TKI-pretreated subgroup);
OptiTROP-Lung03, led by Prof. Li Zhang (sacituzumab tirumotecan vs docetaxel; ORR 45.1% vs 15.6%; median PFS 6.9 vs 2.8 months);
CAMPASS, led by Prof. Baohui Han (benmelstobart plus anlotinib vs pembrolizumab; median PFS 11 vs 7.1 months);
Prof. Yilong Wu publicly questioned NeoADAURA for setting MPR rather than EFS as the primary endpoint; CheckMate 816 reported a 5-year survival rate of 65.4%.

Search public sources to verify the exact data and primary congress materials, then add other influential Chinese expert presentations from the meeting. Re-group everything under these topics: treatment strategy / resistance mechanisms / detection technology / perioperative care. For each, flag the core viewpoint of each expert and where the opinions actually diverge. Deliver a single self-contained HTML radar page where each topic expands into detail, with sources attached.

I have a 15-minute departmental meeting at a chest hospital this Friday, in front of more than 20 medical oncologists, on "Managing Resistance After First-Line Therapy in Advanced EGFR-Mutated NSCLC." I need something I can present straight away: slides plus page-by-page speaker notes.

Here is the real material to work from. Verify the exact sources, current status, and domestic approval situation, and supplement where needed:
Publicly reported highlights from the 2025 ASCO lung cancer sessions:
SACHI, led by Prof. Shun Lu (MET-amplified population; osimertinib plus savolitinib vs platinum-doublet chemotherapy; median PFS 8.2 vs 4.5 months in the ITT population, ORR 58%; median PFS 6.9 months in the third-generation TKI-pretreated subgroup);
OptiTROP-Lung03, led by Prof. Li Zhang (sacituzumab tirumotecan vs docetaxel; ORR 45.1% vs 15.6%; median PFS 6.9 vs 2.8 months);
CAMPASS, led by Prof. Baohui Han (benmelstobart plus anlotinib vs pembrolizumab; median PFS 11 vs 7.1 months);
Prof. Yilong Wu publicly questioned NeoADAURA for setting MPR rather than EFS as the primary endpoint; CheckMate 816 reported a 5-year survival rate of 65.4%.

Give me a deck of around 12 slides with notes for every page. Write the notes the way physicians actually speak — no lecturing — and cite the data source on each slide.

Physicians fire questions at me mid-visit and I lose my footing. Lately they quote Chinese experts' own criticisms from international congresses straight back at me — for example: "You all say combination therapy is great, but didn't Prof. Yilong Wu criticize NeoADAURA at ASCO 2025 for setting MPR rather than EFS as the primary endpoint?" or "HERTHENA-Lung02 with the HER3 ADC fell flat too — is the ADC route even viable?"

Build me a pocket handbook for handling objections: lay out every academic challenge I'm likely to face, and for each one give the publicly verifiable factual basis, how to respond, and where I have to concede that the data isn't mature yet.

Background material — verify and supplement via public sources:
Publicly reported highlights from the 2025 ASCO lung cancer sessions:
SACHI, led by Prof. Shun Lu (MET-amplified population; osimertinib plus savolitinib vs platinum-doublet chemotherapy; median PFS 8.2 vs 4.5 months in the ITT population, ORR 58%; median PFS 6.9 months in the third-generation TKI-pretreated subgroup);
OptiTROP-Lung03, led by Prof. Li Zhang (sacituzumab tirumotecan vs docetaxel; ORR 45.1% vs 15.6%; median PFS 6.9 vs 2.8 months);
CAMPASS, led by Prof. Baohui Han (benmelstobart plus anlotinib vs pembrolizumab; median PFS 11 vs 7.1 months);
Prof. Yilong Wu publicly questioned NeoADAURA for setting MPR rather than EFS as the primary endpoint; CheckMate 816 reported a 5-year survival rate of 65.4%.

Deliver a Word document organized by objection type, one page per entry, with sources cited.

Prompt 1 ｜De Novo Design

I am an antibody researcher working on tumor immunology, targeting PD-L1. Please use the IgGM(WDL) public application with fully default parameters (do not modify the antigen, model, or resource configuration), perform one antibody de novo design (De Novo Design), and complete the analysis:

1. Before submission, give me a task confirmation sheet (design mode | target | key parameters | WDL engine | estimated duration), then submit after confirmation;
2. Track the task until completion; if it fails, provide root cause analysis and fix recommendations based on the error knowledge base;
3. Upon completion, deliver a single-file HTML report (with embedded 3Dmol.js + PDB coordinates): candidate antibody sequence table (rank | VH/VL | developability score); representative candidate 3D interactive view per "3D Delivery Standard" (chain coloring, auto-rotation by default, drag/zoom, chain visibility toggle, representation switch, distance measurement, screenshot).

Prompt 2 ｜ CDR Region Redesign

I have an anti-PD-L1 lead antibody with a humanized and stable framework region. I need to keep the framework region unchanged and redesign the CDR region to improve binding properties. Please use the IgGM(WDL) public application with default parameters to perform CDR Redesign and complete the analysis:

1. Before submission, confirm the design region (default CDR-H3) and parameter summary, then submit after confirmation;
2. Track the task until completion;
3. Deliver the results as a single-file HTML report: before/after CDR comparison table (IMGT numbering | original residue → new residue); run Merge_output post-processing to generate sequence logo and mutation probability histogram (design group vs. original group); interactive 3D view of the redesigned product following the "3D delivery standard" (complex view with antigen 5C3T_A, chain coloring, auto-rotation by default, chain show/hide, antigen surface, distance measurement, screenshot).

Prompt 3 ｜ CDR-H3 Conditional Design

For the default PD-L1 system, please use the IgGM(WDL) public application with all default parameters (do not change any field) to perform one round of CDR-H3 conditional design: use the default antigen as the constraint condition for conditional generation of the CDR-H3 region, and complete the analysis:

1. Before submission, provide a task confirmation sheet (design mode | design region CDR-H3 | target antigen | WDL engine | resources | estimated duration), then submit after confirmation;
2. Track the task until completion;
3. Deliver results as a single-file HTML report: candidate CDR-H3 sequence summary table (sequence | frequency | positional conservation); run Merge_output post-processing to generate CDR-H3 sequence logo and per-position conservation histogram; interactive 3D view of top 1-2 candidates following the "3D delivery standard" (chain coloring, auto-rotation by default, chain show/hide, distance measurement, screenshot).

Prompt 1 | Structure Prediction

I am a researcher in enzyme engineering and have a batch of new sequences I want to quickly visualize for folding structure. Please use the ORI public application's usmfold-predict sub-workflow, following all default parameters (no changes to input, model, or resource configuration), and run a structure prediction on the default example sequence, then complete the analysis:

1. Before submission, provide me with a task confirmation sheet (sub-workflow | input summary | key parameters | estimated duration), then submit after confirmation;
2. Track the task until completion; if it fails, provide root cause analysis and fix suggestions based on the error knowledge base;
3. Upon completion, output: pLDDT confidence statistics (overall mean | N-terminal | core region), and generate a structure prediction HTML report — with an embedded interactive 3D structure (3Dmol.js, PDB data directly embedded in the file): **cartoon + semi-transparent molecular surface overlay**, colored by pLDDT rwb gradient (red=low confidence → blue=high confidence), **auto-rotation enabled by default** (Y-axis, speed 0.5), with three control buttons (auto-rotate / hide surface / reset view) + mouse drag rotation / scroll-to-zoom tips, rendering dynamically when the report is opened.

I have a single-cell proteomics peptide quantification dataset and need to assess peptide quantification reliability. Please use the scPROTEIN application to run Stage1 peptide-level uncertainty quantification with default parameters.

1. Confirm the sub-application, data scale, and parameter summary before submission; submit after my confirmation;
2. Track the task to completion; provide root cause diagnosis on failure;
3. Visualize results: uncertainty distribution histogram (with P90 threshold line), Top20 high-uncertainty peptide chart and review table, high-variance peptide heatmap — open the HTML interactive report in the built-in browser.

Prompt 1｜Antibody Structure Prediction (tFold-Ab) → CDR Quality Assessment

I am a molecular design scientist in antibody drug development. I need the Fv three-dimensional structure of a candidate antibody (7ox3 system VH/VL), with a focus on evaluating CDR-H3 conformation quality to support humanization decisions. Please use the tfold-ab sub-workflow of the tFold public application, run with default parameters, and complete the analysis:

1. Before submission, provide a task confirmation sheet (sub-workflow | design intent | key parameters | estimated duration), then submit after confirmation;
2. Track the task until completion; if it fails, provide root cause analysis and repair suggestions based on the error knowledge base;
3. After completion, output: an HTML report page with a confidence table (lDDT-Ca | pTM | ipTM); **3D display** using 3Dmol.js to embed the predicted structure **inside the report's '3D Structure Display' container (canvas confined within the container, not hovering over other report content; container requires position:relative + overflow:hidden constraints)** — cartoon colored by chain (H blue / L orange) + semi-transparent molecular surface, CDR-H3 loop highlighted in red sticks, **auto-rotation enabled by default**, three buttons ▶ Auto-rotate / ◆ Hide surface / ↻ Reset view, legend 'Chain H Heavy Chain (Blue) | Chain L Light Chain (Orange) | CDR-H3 (Red)', tooltip 'Drag to rotate · Scroll to zoom' (.pth output is actually PDB text, copy as .pdb then embed); load 7ox3 experimental structure from RCSB for comparison.

Prompt 2｜Antibody-Antigen Complex Prediction (tFold-Ag) → Epitope Mapping and Dual-Mode Comparison

I am the structural biology lead for an antiviral antibody project. I need the complex structure of an anti-SARS-CoV-2 RBD antibody Fab with the RBD antigen, to locate the epitope and paratope and guide mutation and affinity engineering. Please use the tFold-Ag sub-workflow (MSA standard mode) of the tFold public application, run with default parameters, and complete the analysis:

1. Before submission, provide a task confirmation sheet (sub-workflow | design intent | key parameters | estimated duration), then submit after confirmation;
2. Track the task until completion; if it fails, provide root cause analysis and repair suggestions based on the error knowledge base;
3. After completion, output: an HTML report page with a confidence table (overall lDDT-Ca | ipTM | pTM | antigen chain lDDT); **3D display** using 3Dmol.js to embed the complex **inside the report's '3D Structure Display' container (canvas confined within the container, not hovering over other report content; container requires position:relative + overflow:hidden constraints)** — default interface highlight view (cartoon colored by chain: RBD antigen green / H blue / L orange; epitope purple+stick, paratope red+stick) + semi-transparent molecular surface, **auto-rotation enabled by default**, three buttons ▶ Auto-rotate / ◆ Hide surface / ↻ Reset view, legend 'Chain A RBD Antigen (Green) | Chain H Heavy Chain (Blue) | Chain L Light Chain (Orange) | Epitope (Purple) | Paratope (Red)', tooltip 'Drag to rotate · Scroll to zoom'; then automatically cascade ICF mode (default parameters) for comparison and output a dual-mode scoring comparison table.

Prompt 3｜TCR-pMHC Structure Prediction (tFold-TCR) → Recognition Interface Validation

I am a researcher in the TCR therapy field. I need the predicted structure of the TCR in the Mycobacterium tuberculosis InhA peptide-HLA-E system (6zkw), to analyze the CDR3 conformation and pMHC recognition interface. Please use the tfold-tcr sub-workflow of the tFold public application, run with default parameters, and complete the analysis:

1. Before submission, provide a task confirmation sheet (sub-workflow | design intent | key parameters | estimated duration), then submit after confirmation;
2. Track the task until completion; if it fails, provide root cause analysis and repair suggestions based on the error knowledge base;
3. After completion, output: an HTML report page with a confidence table (lDDT-Ca | pTM | ipTM); **3D display** using 3Dmol.js to embed the predicted structure **inside the report's '3D Structure Display' container (canvas confined within the container, not hovering over other report content; container requires position:relative + overflow:hidden constraints)** — cartoon colored by chain (α blue / β orange) + semi-transparent molecular surface, CDR3 loop highlighted in red sticks (α 89–97 / β 96–104 indicative range), **auto-rotation enabled by default**, three buttons ▶ Auto-rotate / ◆ Hide surface / ↻ Reset view, legend 'Chain α TRAV (Blue) | Chain β TRBV (Orange) | CDR3 (Red)', tooltip 'Drag to rotate · Scroll to zoom'; load 6zkw experimental structure from RCSB for comparison.

I need to encode gene perturbation data into UniPert 256-dimensional unified representations and evaluate cross-modal neighborhood relationships. Please use the anndata sub-application from the UniPert-WDL collection, with the default input template (anndata_genetic.h5ad, genetic perturbation, no need for me to provide data, pass the template via --input explicitly) to execute perturbation representation encoding.

1. Confirm the sub-application, duplicate name check result, and parameter summary before submission; submit after my confirmation;
2. Track the task to completion; provide root cause diagnosis on failure (debug evidence + error knowledge base matching + fix suggestions);
3. Consolidate results into a reusable ECharts interactive HTML report (e.g., unipert_anndata_report.html), open preview in built-in browser, must include: overview cards (perturbation count / representation dimensions / active dimensions / sparsity / nearest neighbor perturbation / neighborhood similarity), 256-dim representation fingerprint heatmap (peak activation dimensions annotated), cross-modal similarity comparison chart (gene / protein / compound), sparse activation pattern interpretation and conclusions.

Based on the attached technical disclosure document 《注塑机锁模力自适应调节_技术交底书.md》, draft a complete set of patent claims and write all final deliverables to the designated output directory (default ./output/):

