1. 调用【找钢行情MCP】取该品类当前均价及近一周/一月涨跌，查询【行业信息资产库】里这个行业的行情研判口径（淡旺季、限产、库存去化、下游需求），判断价格趋势；
2. 测算：可用天数、安全库存、建议补货量；
3. 给出备货建议：是否补货、补多少、是否分批建仓、锁价还是观望、资金占用比例控制；
4. 给出风险提示与止盈/止损参考。

若行情数据源未就绪或返回不足，请以通用采购与库存管理方法论为主产出并说明。请生成完整备货建议。

cases.prompt_en:
Please use the library capability to clone this workbench in one click: https://workbuddy.link/p/pZcGgLKyjHkHMvNbF5CKI6, with online data storage and two-way sync. Prefer the one-click clone path; if unavailable, build as follows: Build a 'Student Side-Hustle Radar' as a workbench for university students seeking part-time work, internships, and online side hustles. Store all page data in library databases and read/write it at runtime. Do not present local storage, backup, restore, import, or export as product features. Five modules:
1. Home dashboard: Today’s Focus, saved tracks, best fits, in-progress tracks, this week’s tasks, and a connected data table;
2. Opportunity Radar: show opportunity cards and a track library together, with filters for keyword, type, income, time commitment, remote suitability, and more. A user can save an opportunity as a personal track, add or delete tracks, and compare tracks side by side;
3. Find My Fit: collect major, available time, monthly income target, commute, skills, and preferences; recommend tracks by income, flexibility, remote suitability, growth, and resume value;
4. Starter: each track has expandable zero-to-one steps, completion state, due date, first-income record, and preparation checklists for skills, portfolio, and channels;
5. My Progress: summarize active tracks, next steps, nearest due dates, and first-income status. Use five library databases: Opportunity Feed, My Tracks, My Attempts, My Profile, and Connected Data Tables. Each schema must map directly to the page’s read/write fields; opportunities and tracks support create, update, and delete, while attempts and profile support ongoing updates. Include anonymized demo data: about 29 opportunities, 12 tracks, 2 starter records, and 1 rate-reference table. Visual direction: a bright, compact student productivity workbench with a deep blue-purple header, light cards, and clear task-priority and state colors. All CSS, JS, and demo data are inline with no external CDN dependency.

Deliverable: an online Library workbench — an online HTML page plus the data tables deployed to the Library space, with the page bound to the tables for online storage and two-way sync.

cases.prompt:
投完一波广告，帮我出一份完整的、能下载打印的复盘报告（HTML）。

【基本情况】
- 品牌 / 产品：{品牌或店铺名}，{产品和客单价，如「东方香氛香薰蜡烛，168-588 元」}
- 渠道：{腾讯广告朋友圈+视频号 / 抖音巨量 / 小红书 / 千川 / 快手 / 百度}
- 周期：{起始日期} 至 {结束日期}，已结案
- 考核：主要要 {订单 / 线索 / 涨粉}，当初想控制在 {一个多少钱} 以内

【数据】（没有的直接写「无」，不用估算）
- 总花费 {金额}｜结果数 {订单或线索数}｜成交额 {GMV}
- 曝光 / 点击：{曝光量} / {点击量}
- 逐日明细：{每天的日期、消耗、结果数}
- 素材明细：{每条的名称、视频还是图片、卖点、消耗、点击率、结果数}
- 中间调整：{第几天加过预算 / 换过素材 / 改过出价}

【产出】
顶部先用大白话给四段结论（这波的总账 / 做对了什么 / 还能更好的地方 /【下次这样投】行动清单），下面接六节数据文档：01 表现总览 + 成交漏斗｜02 逐日走势折线图（标出爬坡·高峰·衰退三段和成本拐点）｜03 阶段对比 + 效率缺口测算｜04 素材分析（结构 / 排行 / 建议三部分）｜05 五维星级综合评价｜06 下一波建议 + 目标对照。

写到 outputs/ 并打开预览。

cases.prompt_en:
My ad campaign has wrapped up. Please produce a complete, downloadable and print-ready retrospective report (HTML).

[Basics]
- Brand / product: {brand or shop name}, {product and price range, e.g. "Eastern-aesthetic scented candles, 168-588 RMB"}
- Channel: {Tencent Ads WeChat Moments + Channels / Douyin Ocean Engine / Xiaohongshu / Qianchuan / Kuaishou / Baidu}
- Date range: {start date} to {end date}, campaign closed
- Target: primarily {orders / leads / followers}, originally aiming to stay under {target cost per result}

[Data] (write "none" for anything you don't have — do not estimate)
- Total spend {amount} | Results {orders or leads} | Revenue {GMV}
- Impressions / clicks: {impressions} / {clicks}
- Daily breakdown: {date, spend, results for each day}
- Creative breakdown: {name, video or image, selling point, spend, CTR, results for each}
- Mid-flight changes: {which day you raised budget / swapped creatives / adjusted bids}

[Deliverable]
Open with four plain-language conclusions (the bottom line / what worked / what could be better / a numbered "run it this way next time" action list), then six data sections: 01 Performance overview + conversion funnel | 02 Daily trend line chart (marking ramp-up, peak and decline phases plus the cost inflection point) | 03 Phase comparison + efficiency gap analysis | 04 Creative analysis (structure / ranking / recommendations) | 05 Five-dimension star rating | 06 Next-round recommendations + target benchmarks.

Write it to outputs/ and open a preview.

Please use the Library capability to make a one-click copy of https://www.workbuddy.cn/space/d/FCtGCs9SZKxZEWrQfS29BE?source=2 with online data storage and bidirectional sync. Prioritize the one-click replication flow; if that is unavailable, build it as follows: Build a long-term Teacher Workspace for primary and secondary school teachers in China. One teacher should be able to manage multiple classes. The goal is to complete a round of student records in 30 seconds during class, then review summaries, grades, and tasks after class. Create and connect ten online tables: Students, Schedule, Projects, Academic Records, Behavior Records, Tasks, Attendance, Family Contacts, Communication Records, and Class Duties. Calculate every summary from raw records in real time. Creates, updates, and deletes must write back to Library and synchronize in the page. Include:
1. Today: daily schedule, unfinished tasks, and students pending retest;
2. Quick Record: choose a class, date, and project, then select students to record completion, scores, passing status, or behavior points in batches;
3. Insights: completion rate, latest exam mean, pass rate, behavior trends, and pending retests;
4. Grades: latest valid score for each student by class and assessment;
5. Roster: browse and search students by class and tags;
6. Homeroom: attendance exceptions, family contacts, communication records, and class duties. Use a light, clear, highly readable teacher-workflow style. Use a wide multi-column desktop layout and a responsive single-column mobile layout. Chinese is the default language and the English interface must be complete. Demo data must be anonymized; family phone numbers, notes, and communication content may appear only on homeroom-related pages. Deliver a single HTML file Online storage and bidirectional sync must remain the only data product model.

Deliverable: an online Library workbench — an online HTML page plus the data tables deployed to the Library space, with the page bound to the tables for online storage and two-way sync.

cases.prompt:
你是TradeBuddy出品的B2B贸易销售专家。请帮我生成一套营销推广内容。

【背景】
- 公司：{如 华东建材贸易}
- 主推：{如 螺纹/高线/板卷现货，当天送达}
- 主题/卖点：{如 现货充足、含税到货、材质质保齐全}

【要求】
1. 结合当前行情氛围（可调用【找钢行情MCP】），查询【行业信息资产库】里这个行业的营销话术口径；
2. 生成一整套：①公众号推文（标题+导语）②朋友圈短文案3条 ③海报文案（主标题+副标题+CTA，可交设计出图）；
3. 文案要贴合钢铁/建材贸易场景、突出现货和信任感、口语接地气、有紧迫感。

请生成完整营销内容套件。

cases.prompt_en:
Using the medication-safety capabilities of the Tencent Health AI Clinical Assistant, help me screen polypharmacy risk for an elderly patient:

My dad is 72, with hypertension, atrial fibrillation and diabetes. He takes warfarin, metoprolol, metformin and aspirin daily. Lately his gums bleed and he bruises easily. Please assess:
1. Which drug combination most likely explains the bleeding tendency (focus: anticoagulant + antiplatelet stacking);
2. Which symptoms are danger signs needing immediate care (black stools, hematemesis, hematuria, persistent bleeding, altered consciousness, chest pain) versus mild watchable symptoms;
3. Next steps (see a doctor for PT/INR, bring the full medication list) and explain why anticoagulants should not be stopped on your own.

Strictly separate emergency signs from watchable symptoms. Do not recommend stopping or adjusting anticoagulant/antiplatelet or chronic glucose-lowering drugs on your own. Do not give specific dose-adjustment numbers. End with a recommendation to see a doctor promptly to check coagulation.

Prompt 2 | De Novo Design → Structure Validation

I am a protein designer in the industrial enzyme field, targeting a thermostable bifunctional enzyme (chitinase + lysozyme activity) that can withstand 60°C. Please use the ORI public application's generate-protein sub-workflow, following all default parameters (default design prompt, model, and resource configuration), and run a de novo protein design, then complete the analysis:

1. Before submission, provide me with a task confirmation sheet (sub-workflow | design intent | key parameters | estimated duration), then submit after confirmation;
2. Track the task until completion; if it fails, provide root cause analysis and fix suggestions based on the error knowledge base;
3. Upon completion, output: candidate sequence table (rank | name | length | score), rendered as an HTML report page; then automatically cascade usmfold-predict (default parameters) on the top-scoring candidate, with its predicted structure embedded in the report's 3D area (3Dmol.js, PDB data embedded): **cartoon + semi-transparent surface overlay**, colored by pLDDT rwb, **auto-rotation enabled by default**, with 3 control buttons (auto-rotate / hide surface / reset view) + mouse interaction tips, directly interactive within the report; also provide the PDB file for deep analysis in Mol*.

I have completed Stage1 peptide-level uncertainty quantification and now need to learn cell embeddings for cluster annotation. Please use the scPROTEIN application to run Stage2 cell embedding with default parameters.

1. Confirm that Stage1 output is readable, along with data scale and parameter summary before submission; submit after my confirmation;
2. Track the task to completion; provide root cause diagnosis on failure;
3. Visualize results: PCA→t-SNE cell cluster scatter plot (KMeans colored), Silhouette vs k curve with optimal k, PCA variance explained plot — open the HTML interactive report in the built-in browser.

I need to perform compound MOA clustering and mechanism of action analysis through unified perturbation representations. Please use the compounds sub-application from the UniPert-WDL collection, with the default input template (compounds.csv, SMILES input, no need for me to provide data) to execute compound representation encoding, then perform hierarchical clustering and MOA determination based on cosine similarity.

1. Confirm the sub-application, duplicate name check result, and parameter summary before submission; submit after my confirmation;
2. Track the task to completion; provide root cause diagnosis on failure (debug evidence + error knowledge base matching + fix suggestions);
3. Consolidate results into a reusable ECharts interactive HTML report (e.g., unipert_moa_report.html), open preview in built-in browser, must include: overview cards (compound count / representation dimensions / MOA category count / cluster pair similarity / Top-20 overlapping dimensions / runtime), clustering heatmap + dendrogram (with same-class threshold line 0.30 and determination conclusion panel), Top activation dimension comparison chart (shared activation dimensions highlighted in amber), known pharmacology cross-validation table (model determination vs known MOA + consistency labels), cross-modal reference chart (endogenous vs exogenous separation), conclusions and application value (drug repurposing / combination drug screening / MOA annotation).

Using the medication-safety capabilities of the Tencent Health AI Clinical Assistant, evaluate a patient's risk of combining warfarin with supplements:/n/nThe patient has been on warfarin long-term and now plans to self-add fish oil, ginkgo leaf supplements and panax powder. Please assess:/n1. The bleeding risk after combining them (focus: the antiplatelet / anticoagulant activity of fish oil, ginkgo and panax stacks with warfarin, possibly raising INR);
2. Whether any combination is contraindicated or should be avoided (itemize: which to avoid, which to use cautiously, which to use with careful monitoring);
3. INR monitoring recommendations (baseline INR, follow-up timing after adding, target range);
4. Patient counseling (bleeding warning signs, when to seek care, medication adherence, not stopping on their own).

Objectively explain the interaction mechanism. Do not flatly dismiss the value of traditional Chinese medicines / supplements. Do not recommend stopping warfarin or other anticoagulants on your own (stopping carries thrombotic risk). Flag the bleeding risk proactively rather than waiting for the user to ask. End with a recommendation to defer to a doctor / pharmacist.

Prompt 3 | Thermostability Assessment · Design Validation

I am an engineer in the fermentation process field and need to confirm whether a protein's thermal tolerance meets the 60°C process requirement. Please use the ORI public application's thermostability sub-workflow, following all default parameters (default example input, model, and resource configuration), and run a thermostability assessment, then complete the analysis:

1. Before submission, provide me with a task confirmation sheet (sub-workflow | input summary | key parameters | estimated duration), then submit after confirmation;
2. Track the task until completion; if it fails, provide root cause analysis and fix suggestions based on the error knowledge base;
3. Upon completion, output: predicted Tm result table (sequence | predicted Tm(°C) | 60°C threshold judgment), and render an HTML validation report (pass/fail + margin annotation); advanced usage: when following Prompt 2, switch to using its top candidate sequence as input (model and resources still default) to verify whether the '60°C-tolerant' design goal has been achieved.

I need to fully demonstrate scPROTEIN end-to-end capability: starting from the default public dataset, run Stage1 (uncertainty quantification) and Stage2 (cell embedding) sequentially, and deliver a visualization report. Both stages use default parameters.

1. Confirm both sub-applications and parameter summary before submission; submit after my confirmation;
2. After Stage1 completes and output is validated, then submit Stage2; provide root cause diagnosis for any failure;
3. Consolidate results into a reusable ECharts interactive HTML report file (e.g., scprotein_visual_report.html), open preview in built-in browser, must include: overview cards (peptide count/cell count/embedding dimension/optimal k/silhouette/low-confidence ratio), t-SNE cell cluster scatter plot (KMeans colored + Silhouette vs k curve), uncertainty distribution histogram (P90 threshold line), Top20 review table, high-variance peptide heatmap.

I need to complete protein multi-level classification based on UniPert unified representations. Please use the genes sub-application from the UniPert-WDL collection, with the default input template (protein.fasta, no need for me to provide data) to execute protein representation encoding.

1. Confirm the sub-application, duplicate name check result, and parameter summary before submission; submit after my confirmation;
2. Track the task to completion; provide root cause diagnosis on failure (debug evidence + error knowledge base matching + fix suggestions);
3. Consolidate results into a reusable ECharts interactive HTML report (e.g., unipert_protein_report.html), open preview in built-in browser, must include: overview cards (protein count / representation dimensions / active dimensions / nearest neighbor perturbation / neighborhood similarity / hierarchical classification results), three-level classification hierarchy diagram (perturbation modality layer → representation neighborhood layer → activation feature layer, with rationale for each level), representation fingerprint heatmap (peak dimensions annotated), neighborhood similarity comparison chart, classification basis summary and limitations.

Using the medication-safety capabilities of the Tencent Health AI Clinical Assistant, evaluate a patient's drug-related bleeding risk and the possibility of overdose:

A 72-year-old man with hypertension, atrial fibrillation and diabetes has been on warfarin, metoprolol, metformin and aspirin long-term. Recently he has recurrent gum bleeding and subcutaneous bruising. Please assess:
1. Whether there is a drug-related bleeding risk (focus: warfarin 'anticoagulant' + aspirin 'antiplatelet' stack to raise bleeding risk);
2. Whether overdose is possible (focus: whether gum bleeding + bruising signals excessive anticoagulation / an elevated INR — needs coagulation testing to judge, rather than simply calling it 'too many drugs');
3. Which are danger signs needing immediate care (black stools, hematemesis, hematuria, persistent bleeding, headache or altered consciousness, chest pain) versus mild watchable symptoms;
4. Next steps (see a doctor promptly for PT/INR, bring the full medication list), and explain why anticoagulant / antiplatelet drugs must not be stopped on one's own (stopping raises stroke / thrombotic risk in AF).

Objectively explain the bleeding mechanism and the basis for judging overdose. Do not recommend stopping or adjusting anticoagulant/antiplatelet or chronic glucose-lowering drugs on your own. Do not give specific dose-adjustment numbers. Flag the bleeding risk proactively. End with a recommendation to see a doctor promptly to check coagulation.

I'm the product lead for a mid-market enterprise CRM SaaS. Please help me run through a complete brainstorming and idea-screening exercise for AI assistant use cases:
1) Around the five dimensions of "sales effectiveness, customer success, data intelligence, automation, and collaboration," produce 18 candidate AI use cases;
2) Use a value/cost matrix (high value low cost, high value high cost, low value low cost, low value high cost) to screen the 18 use cases and output a Top 5;
3) Write feature outlines for the Top 5 (user stories, core interactions, data dependencies, success metrics);
4) Based on the differences in AI capabilities across Salesforce / HubSpot / Zoho / Feishu, provide a competitive differentiation strategy;
5) Provide tiered pricing recommendations for AI features (Free Basic / Pro / Enterprise).
Finally, output a Markdown report + an HTML visualization page.

I'm the product lead for a mid-market CRM SaaS company. Please help me write the 2026 Q1 stakeholder (CEO / executive team / board) quarterly review. The content should include:
1) Progress on core metrics (North Star NRR 103%→106%, plus MRR / ARR / NDR / Churn / CAC Payback, etc.);
2) Q1 roadmap delivery status (against the agreed OKRs, 6/8 achieved, 2 delayed, with reasons and impact explained);
3) Key AI MVP data (adoption rate, retention, user feedback);
4) 3-5 major wins and lessons learned;
5) Q2 priorities and key risks;
6) Resource needs (headcount / budget / external partnerships);
7) A list of resolutions requested from the board.
Final output: a Markdown quarterly review plus an HTML visualization page (a core-metrics dashboard + a roadmap status wall).

A Hong Kong stock, Meituan-W (3690.HK), released a worse-than-expected quarterly report last night, and is down 8% pre-market today. I had planned to buy today. Please make a rapid decision analysis.

Markdown report requirements:
1. Interpretation of the core earnings data (revenue, profit, segment data);
2. News and industry reactions (institutional rating adjustments, peer reactions);
3. Technical breakdown levels and key supports;
4. Main capital flow direction (southbound, changes in institutional holdings);
5. A clear conclusion after weighing bull vs. bear: whether to chase today, at what price to chase, and how much position size.

I've worked at an internet company for 5 years and 3 months. Last month the company unilaterally reassigned me from "Product Director" to "Product Assistant" and cut my monthly salary from 30,000 to 12,000. I did not agree, and now the company assigns me trivial work that doesn't match my position every day. I'm considering claiming constructive dismissal (forced resignation) and demanding economic compensation.

Please handle this using the full Chinese legal consultation team workflow:
1. First do information gathering, and ask me follow-up questions when essential information is missing;
2. Once information is sufficient, output a complete "Legal Consultation Report" in Markdown that must include: case summary, applicable statutes (Labor Contract Law / Labor Law / Civil Code / Supreme People's Court interpretations), 3-5 similar precedents, legal characterization, assessment of the chances of winning, recommended courses of action (negotiation / arbitration / litigation), risk and statute-of-limitations reminders, and recommended next steps;
3. Separately attach an "Evidence Collection Checklist" telling me which evidence I need to preserve going forward;
4. Please clearly explain how to calculate the economic compensation, the wage differential, and any possible additional/punitive damages.

My wife and I have been married for 8 years and have a 6-year-old child. During the marriage we jointly bought an apartment (the property deed is registered solely under my name, the ¥600,000 down payment was paid by my parents, and we both repay the mortgage together), a car (registered under my wife's name), and we have some investments. We are now preparing to divorce, and I want the apartment and custody of the child, and I am willing to pay reasonable compensation.

Please handle this using the ChatLaw Team's complete workflow:
1. First conduct information intake, and follow up with me when necessary information is missing;
2. Output a complete Legal Consultation Report in Markdown, which must include: case summary, applicable statutes, similar precedents, legal characterization, property division outcome ranges (negotiated divorce vs. litigated divorce), factors influencing the custody decision, recommended path (negotiation → mediation → litigation), risk warnings, and an evidence checklist;
3. Clearly identify which assets are marital property and which may be considered personal property or personal contributions;
4. Explain, if the apartment is awarded to me, roughly how the compensation would be calculated;
5. Provide next-step action recommendations.

I want to build a mobile app called "Wordbox" (frontend in React Native), with a target audience of young people preparing for graduate school entrance exams / studying abroad. Core need: learn vocabulary through AI conversation for 15 minutes a day, supporting the Ebbinghaus review curve, a vocabulary notebook, daily check-ins, a check-in calendar, and study statistics.

Please complete the full end-to-end delivery from 0 to 1:
1. A complete PRD (goals, user stories, competitor analysis, feature list with priorities, open questions to confirm);
2. System architecture design (technology choices, module breakdown, core data structures, interface definitions, sequence diagrams);
3. A task breakdown list (sorted by dependency, logical analysis of each file, shared knowledge, API Spec);
4. Runnable engineering code (frontend pages + local storage + an integration layer for the AI conversation interface);
5. Complete unit/integration test cases and a test report.

Deliver in the form of an engineering directory + Markdown documents, and finally summarize a project delivery summary.

I have a PR with 3000+ lines of changes (a backend Go service, the core logic of the order module + a small database schema adjustment). Please do a comprehensive code review.

Requirements:
- Cover the four dimensions of security, performance, correctness, and maintainability;
- Assess the impact on the existing architecture;
- Assess test coverage and the adequacy of the test cases;
- Sort findings by severity (Blocker / Major / Minor / Suggestion);
- For each comment, give the specific location, a description of the problem, and a suggested fix.

Output a complete "PR Review Report" Markdown document + a condensed version that can be pasted directly into the PR comments.

We're building a new feature, an "in-app AI assistant" (within a SaaS product, where users ask questions in natural language and the AI queries internal data and provides answers). A PRD draft already exists; please conduct a complete review:
- Product review: four independent reviews from the CEO (business value), Design (experience), Engineering (complexity), and DX (developer experience);
- Security audit: a dual-perspective assessment using OWASP + STRIDE (prompt injection, data leakage, privilege escalation, etc.);
- QA strategy: a test plan, automation-coverage recommendations, and a canary release plan;
- Design review: whether the visual mockups and interactions conform to the design system, and any improvable variants.

Output a Markdown "In-App AI Assistant Feature Complete Review Report", segmented and signed by each reviewer, with each section giving clear improvement items and a Go/No-Go recommendation.

Two years ago I bought 10,000 shares of BYD (002594.SZ) at 25 yuan; I'm now down 30% and have been unable to bring myself to cut my losses. Please organize an investment-research roundtable discussion and tell me:

1. How are the fundamentals really doing now, and is there still a thesis;
2. Technically, are the conditions in place for buying the dip in batches, and if so, where are the support levels;
3. The stance of capital flows (northbound, institutions) — are they buying or selling;
4. The differing short-term and medium-term views;
5. Finally, give me three response plans in different styles (aggressive averaging-down / conservative holding / stop-loss and rotation).

Output a Markdown roundtable summary, with viewpoints from different perspectives clearly signed (Industry Strategist / Chief Signal Trader / Valuation Analyst / Contrarian Investor / Fundamentals Researcher / Short-Term Surfer); preserve the disagreements, don't smooth them over. Then append an HTML version, visualized as a "Multi-Perspective Decision Map" (a stance matrix + key price levels + a comparison card for the three plans; single-file, with inline styles or CDN ECharts both acceptable).

A friend recommended I keep an eye on a seemingly under-the-radar ChiNext small cap, saying it "has a big thesis but hasn't been discovered yet." Please organize a roundtable discussion among 6 stock experts to help me tell whether it's the real deal:

1. Fundamentals deep-dive (business mix, financial health, management);
2. Supply-chain position and industry prosperity, compared with peers;
3. Whether the valuation is genuinely cheap or cheap for a reason (PE/PB percentile, PEG);
4. Whether capital has already entered (northbound flows, institutional research visits, top-ten shareholders, the Dragon-Tiger list);
5. Whether the signals have already triggered (weekly chart pattern, volume, breakout levels);
6. Each expert's final stance (Buy / Wait / Pass) and rationale.

Output a Markdown roundtable memo: 6 experts clearly signed by name, disagreements preserved rather than smoothed over, with a "Final Stance Matrix" at the end (each person's Buy/Wait/Pass + one-line rationale), and a concluding final line (who's most bullish / who's most bearish / what the consensus is / what the disagreement is).

The CSI 300 has recently rebounded quickly to 4,200 points. Please organize a roundtable discussion among 6 stock experts on the current market position:

1. The macro and industry perspective;
2. Valuation level (PE, PB percentiles, stating the percentile over how many years of history);
3. The signal side (trend strength, volume/energy, style);
4. The attitude of capital (northbound funds, margin financing, public fund positions);
5. Structural opportunities for the short term and the medium term;
6. If increasing positions, where to allocate; if reducing positions, which to cut first.

Output a Markdown roundtable summary (signed by the 6 experts, with disagreements preserved) + a single-file HTML "Market Thermometer Dashboard" (a large thermometer gauge at the top + 6 sub-dimension sub-scales + position-increase/decrease comparison cards on the right + a vote bar from the 6 experts at the bottom + a dark background; CDN ECharts may be used).

I have ¥500,000 RMB to invest in A-shares, plan to hold 5-10 stocks, target a reasonable return over 3-5 years, and can tolerate a 20-25% drawdown. Please organize a roundtable discussion among 6 stock experts and provide a "core + satellite" portfolio recommendation:

1. What to use for the core positions (a valuation perspective + a contrarian perspective);
2. What to use for the satellite positions (industry + short-term trading);
3. The overlay of consensus direction from the capital-flow side;
4. Risk points and stop-loss conditions at the signal level;
5. Each member gives the 1-2 targets they're most bullish on along with a recommended position size (with specific tickers).

Output a Markdown portfolio recommendation document (user profile / 6 experts' signatures / a final portfolio table including ticker, position, role, and stop-loss / three tiers of rebalancing triggers / a disagreement note) + a single-file HTML portfolio visualization dashboard (a weight pie chart + a six-dimension style radar + a rebalancing-trigger table + a wall of cards for the 6 experts' recommended targets, with a dark background, and ECharts via CDN is allowed).

The AI computing power theme has been very hot lately, and Zhongji Innolight (300308.SZ) is up 25% in a week. Please organize a roundtable discussion among 6 stock experts:

1. Whether the industry trend is real (optical module demand, 800G/1.6T progress, NVIDIA/Google/Meta customer orders);
2. The current valuation percentile — is it reasonable or stretched (PE/PB percentile, PEG, historical bands);
3. The strength and sustainability of the short-term theme;
4. Whether the capital is institution-led or hot-money-driven (northbound flows, the Dragon-Tiger list, turnover rate);
5. If one were to participate, at what price, what position size, and under what circumstances to cut losses.

Output a Markdown roundtable memo (with each expert's signature, disagreements preserved rather than smoothed over) + a single-file HTML "chase or skip" decision card (two side-by-side comparison cards / an industry-truth four-quadrant / a 6-expert mini stance bar / dark background / CDN ECharts allowed).

I'm a brand-new investor just getting started. Please use BYD (002594.SZ) as a case study to create a "step-by-step tutorial on how to systematically analyze a stock."

